WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:09.720
Nice!
But [Laughs]

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.225
$40,000 of those
have been in the last six weeks.

00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:14.309
-Wow.
-Oh, nice.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:15.936
Greiner: And why is that?
What happened?

00:00:15.936 --> 00:00:17.145
You know,
we're very young.

00:00:17.145 --> 00:00:19.482
We have no business
or marketing experience,

00:00:19.482 --> 00:00:20.692
and it took us a long time

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:22.402
to really figure out
what worked, what doesn't.

00:00:22.402 --> 00:00:24.779
Originally, I was like, "Oh,
we'll just run Facebook ads.

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:25.906
That'll -- That'll do it."

00:00:25.906 --> 00:00:27.950
That's not how it works.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.620
And so what we found
we were missing

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.001
was website optimization
and social media marketing,

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:37.544
and we really figured out

00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:40.798
how to do the social media
marketing in March,

00:00:40.798 --> 00:00:43.301
and then in April,
we redid our website.

00:00:43.301 --> 00:00:45.094
And then in June,
we put those together

00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:46.637
for an explosion
of sales,

00:00:46.637 --> 00:00:47.639
and they've been
trending upwards.

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:51.143
So we've had
4,500 in May,

00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:54.314
17,000 in June,
and 20,000 in July.

00:00:54.314 --> 00:00:56.065
Corcoran: Good for you.
Yeah, baby!
That's awesome.

00:00:56.065 --> 00:00:58.026
Greiner:
That's really great.
What did you spend to get that?

00:00:58.026 --> 00:00:59.277
And it's just
the two of you

00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:01.280
running the company
together now?
Yes.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.282
How much did you invest
in the company?

00:01:03.282 --> 00:01:06.243
So, we funded this company
in three different ways,

00:01:06.243 --> 00:01:07.578
and the first way,

00:01:07.578 --> 00:01:09.247
with all due respect,
Mr. Wonderful,

00:01:09.247 --> 00:01:12.584
we like to call our parents
Mr. and Mrs. Wonderful.

00:01:12.584 --> 00:01:13.918
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.918 --> 00:01:16.672
You can call them that, but they
have to pay me a royalty.

00:01:16.672 --> 00:01:18.174
If we make a deal,
then maybe.

00:01:18.174 --> 00:01:19.675
Well,
they believed in us,

00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:22.511
and they helped us with $18,000
to start the business.

00:01:22.511 --> 00:01:23.889
So, the other two ways,

00:01:23.889 --> 00:01:25.140
the first one was

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.142
through an Indiegogo
crowdfunding campaign,

00:01:27.142 --> 00:01:28.769
where we raised $12,000,

00:01:28.769 --> 00:01:30.855
and through all four
pitch competitions

00:01:30.855 --> 00:01:33.524
that we competed in
and won $15,000.

00:01:33.524 --> 00:01:34.901
You did?
Corcoran: Wow.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.319
Have you been
knocked off yet?

00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:37.780
'Cause this
isn't patentable.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.490
No, we have
a utility patent pending.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.033
For a cover on a drink?
Greiner: Is it patentable?

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.159
So, the utility patent

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.286
is for a drink-spiking
prevention device

00:01:44.286 --> 00:01:45.538
coming out
of a wearable.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.374
That's good.
That's great. That's great.

00:01:47.374 --> 00:01:50.251
I'm gonna just jump right in
right here, right now.

00:01:50.251 --> 00:01:52.463
I love this.

00:01:52.463 --> 00:01:55.216
I don't think that
I have ever seen a product

00:01:55.216 --> 00:01:58.511
come into the Shark Tank
that resonated to me more deeply

00:01:58.511 --> 00:02:02.599
in a social mission way
as this.
Wow.

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:05.352
Yep.
I am worried constantly
for young women,

00:02:05.352 --> 00:02:07.897
where women are getting
their drinks drugged,

00:02:07.897 --> 00:02:09.816
they're getting
assaulted.

00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:12.735
It's a horrible thing,
and it's super common,

00:02:12.735 --> 00:02:14.655
and I think
this is genius.

00:02:14.655 --> 00:02:17.199
So I'm gonna
make you an offer.

00:02:17.199 --> 00:02:20.119
I'm gonna offer you
$60,000,

00:02:20.119 --> 00:02:22.330
and I'm gonna do it
just for 25%.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.499
Just 5% more.

00:02:24.499 --> 00:02:26.918
I want to be a partner
right in there with you,

00:02:26.918 --> 00:02:29.004
and I want to do
everything I can

00:02:29.004 --> 00:02:31.715
to actually blow this up,
out on social media,

00:02:31.715 --> 00:02:32.925
create videos.

00:02:32.925 --> 00:02:34.845
This needs to be
in every woman's hands.

00:02:34.845 --> 00:02:37.639
So, I hope that you hear
 my passion about it

00:02:37.639 --> 00:02:38.932
and that you take my offer.

00:02:38.932 --> 00:02:40.725
That means so much.
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:02:40.725 --> 00:02:42.645
I've never heard
Lori that passionate.

00:02:42.645 --> 00:02:43.980
I didn't know she had it
in her blood.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.940
You better
grab that offer and run.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.651
♪

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:49.820
Three, two, one.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.864
Lori, you got a deal.
Lori, you have a deal.

00:02:51.864 --> 00:02:53.615
Yay!
Corcoran: Good choice.

00:02:53.615 --> 00:02:54.658
Kudos to you.

00:02:54.658 --> 00:02:56.911
Fantastic. So smart.

00:02:56.911 --> 00:02:58.288
You have somebody who's really
passionate about it.

00:02:58.288 --> 00:02:59.289
Thank you so much.
Thank you so much.

00:02:59.289 --> 00:03:00.790
Looking forward
to working with you.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.625
Cuban: Well done.
Great idea.
Shirah: Thank you.

00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:03.878
Greiner: Great idea.
Great idea.

00:03:03.878 --> 00:03:06.046
Came to you in a dream,
and now you have $60,000.

00:03:06.046 --> 00:03:07.131
And you know what else?

00:03:07.131 --> 00:03:08.299
You should go to bed
early tonight

00:03:08.299 --> 00:03:09.425
and see what else
you dream up.

00:03:09.425 --> 00:03:11.136
[ Laughter ]
Will do.

00:03:11.136 --> 00:03:12.554
Cuban: Congratulations, guys.
Alright.
Thank you so much.

00:03:12.554 --> 00:03:13.805
Thank you so much.
Looking forward
to working with you.

00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:15.599
Greiner: Congrats.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:17.100
That was pretty fast.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.978
[ Laughs ]

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:20.521
Lori got this right
from the beginning.

00:03:20.521 --> 00:03:21.898
We're so excited
to work with her

00:03:21.898 --> 00:03:22.899
and spread this
around the world.

00:03:22.899 --> 00:03:24.108
We're gonna save
so many lives,

00:03:24.108 --> 00:03:26.111
and we're so excited.
00:03:26.039,00:00:00.000
[ Chuckles ]

